<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1867</h1><p class="ref-lede">1867 in world history: 34 events, 16 births, 26 deaths, 1 work, 8 states founded and 13 that came to an end. 1,022 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a><a href="/years/1864">1864</a><a href="/years/1865">1865</a><a href="/years/1866">1866</a><a href="/years/1867" aria-current="page">1867</a><a href="/years/1868">1868</a><a href="/years/1869">1869</a><a href="/years/1870">1870</a><a href="/years/1871">1871</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-7">7 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fire at the Kingstree jail in South Carolina kills 22 freedmen</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A fire at the jail of Kingstree, the seat of Williamsburg County, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, killed 22 prisoners, 19 men and 3 women. One white prisoner escaped, but every African-American prisoner, held on the third floor, died; attempts at rescue failed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria signs the British North America Act</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The act united the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> and New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a> of Canada. Confederation took effect on 1 July, now Canada Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/canada">Canada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominion</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-30">30 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">United States agrees to buy Alaska from Russia</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">William Seward signed a treaty to buy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> for 7.2 million dollars, about two cents an acre. Mocked as 'Seward's Folly', it proved rich in gold, fish and oil.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-19">19 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Maximilian of Mexico is executed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Maximilian, the Austrian archduke installed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> as Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, was shot by firing squad at Querétaro with two of his generals. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-juarez">Benito Juárez</a>'s republic was restored.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-18">18 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The United States takes possession of Alaska</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sitka">Sitka</a>, the Russian flag was lowered and the US flag raised, formally transferring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a>, bought for 7.2 million dollars. Critics mocked the deal as 'Seward's Folly' until gold and oil proved its value.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mentana" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mentana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-3">3 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">French and papal troops defeat Garibaldi at Mentana</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Mentana, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, papal troops supported by a French expeditionary force defeated the volunteers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a>, who were trying to seize Rome. The victory, aided by the new French Chassepot rifle, kept Rome under the pope until 1870.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mentana">Battle of Mentana</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-garibaldi">Giuseppe Garibaldi</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warsaw.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-7">7 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Marie Curie is born in Warsaw</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Maria Skłodowska was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, then under Russian rule. As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-curie">Marie Curie</a> she pioneered research on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/radioactivity">radioactivity</a> and became the first person to win <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prizes</a> in two sciences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-4">4 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The National Grange is founded</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Oliver Kelley and colleagues founded the Order of Patrons of Husbandry, known as the Grange, in Washington. It became a powerful voice for farmers against railway rates and monopolies.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/keelung" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/keelung.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-18">18 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and tsunami strike Keelung and Taipei in Taiwan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.0 earthquake off northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> seriously damaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keelung">Keelung</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taipei">Taipei</a>, and its tsunami drowned hundreds; the death toll was estimated at 580. It is possibly the only confirmed widely destructive and deadly tsunami in Taiwan's history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keelung">Keelung</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taipei">Taipei</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">Austro-Hungarian Compromise of 1867</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Austro-Hungarian Compromise of 1867, or Ausgleich, was the agreement between the Habsburg monarchy and Hungary that created the dual monarchy of Austria-Hungary.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fandane-thiouthioune" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fandane-thiouthioune.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fandane-thiouthioune">Battle of Fandane-Thiouthioune</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Fandane-Thiouthioune, also called the Battle of Somb, was fought on 18 July 1867 in the kingdom of Sine in present-day Senegal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/luxembourg-crisis" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luxembourg-crisis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/luxembourg-crisis">Luxembourg Crisis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Luxembourg Crisis of 1867 was a diplomatic confrontation between France and Prussia over the status of Luxembourg.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1867" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1867.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-london-1867">Treaty of London (1867)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of London of 11 May 1867 settled the Luxembourg Crisis between France and Prussia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Siege</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kansala">Battle of Kansala</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Kansala was the siege of Kansala, capital of the Kaabu Empire, in 1867 by Fula forces from Futa Jallon and allies.</p></div></li></ol></section>
